  "worked_solution": "In the model, we have $\\frac{2}{5}$ on the left.\n\nSince we need to multiply by $\\frac{3}{4}$, we split the whole into $4$ equal parts horizontally and ensure that $3$ of the parts remain shaded.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14130839/assets/7f79cdedc4fe020369e25f271769304093f7a92be0f507bb54a566ba2b4c3ce8.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents $\\frac{6}{20}$ of the whole.\n\nTherefore, the missing picture is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14130839/assets/6b680d4914abad66b0fb3dd1ee9285a0c00916787b64641eb473fda2366a8053.png)",
